gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-04T16:14:07Z","updated_at":"2025-06-04T16:14:07Z","body":"@lyuma This code can't call `gltf_skeleton->get_godot_skeleton()` because this runs before the Skeleton3D is generated. We also can't call the Node `.get_path_to()` function for the same reason.\r\n\r\n`GLTFDocument::_import_animation` is called after the node tree is generated, we can't use the same techniques in `GLTFNode::get_scene_node_path` because it is called before the node tree is generated.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2940619786/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2954288992","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104787#issuecomment-2954288992","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104787","id":2954288992,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6wFt9g","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-08T21:41:41Z","updated_at":"2025-06-08T21:41:41Z","body":"@lyuma That's true, but it gets really tricky. Also, that would change the function signature, breaking API compatibility with Godot 4.4. Would you be against merging this improvement as-is, and then we can improve it more later if needed?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2954288992/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2955317045","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104787#issuecomment-2955317045","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104787","id":2955317045,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6wJo81","user":{"login":"lyuma","id":39946030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ2MDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma","html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-09T10:05:58Z","updated_at":"2025-06-09T10:05:58Z","body":"> Would you be against merging this improvement as-is\r\n\r\nMy concern is, with the code as written, this is fixing the node path to skinned meshes for UV animation, but at the same time, it is potentially breaking transform paths (rotation, scale...)  Since you can only have one path per gltf node, we have to choose between one or the other, unless we add that extra argument.\r\n\r\nI might prefer to focus for now on the bugfix part of this that does not change the API. For now, we can add the method with the extra argument but only from within Godot C++, but don't expose this extra argument in the public API for now. This will allow us to solve some of the corner cases with skeleton bone transforms and skinned meshes, while keeping the old public API for other properties.\r\n\r\nThis way also, this change can be structured as a bugfix which doesn't add any new APIs, so we can continue to work on this during beta. (If the API change is small enough, we can make a separate PR to expose it later)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2955317045/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3048378117","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104787#issuecomment-3048378117","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104787","id":3048378117,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61so8F","user":{"login":"MeanBeanMachine2024","id":142996610,"node_id":"U_kgDOCIX0gg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/142996610?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeanBeanMachine2024","html_url":"https://github.com/MeanBeanMachine2024","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeanBeanMachine2024/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeanBeanMachine2024/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeanBeanMachine2024/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeanBeanMachine2024/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeanBeanMachine2024/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeanBeanMachine2024/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeanBeanMachine2024/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeanBeanMachine2024/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeanBeanMachine2024/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-08T10:46:22Z","updated_at":"2025-07-08T10:46:22Z","body":"If the code is messy I'd still want messy fix over no fix at all. I am planning on using a character from Blender to Godot that uses multiple animated UV transforms (each eye pupil, facial expressions, etc) and not having to animate that in-engine would really benefit me and others. Even if it's in the last Beta or even RC.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3048378117/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3050136705","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104787#issuecomment-3050136705","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104787","id":3050136705,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61zWSB","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-08T19:54:38Z","updated_at":"2025-07-08T19:54:38Z","body":"> Even if it's in the last Beta or even RC.\r\n\r\nWe entered feature freeze around June 2025 and since this is not fixing a release blocker. This fix node path to skined mesh fix will have to go through the 4.6+ Godot Engine release cycle.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3050136705/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3050334103","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104787#issuecomment-3050334103","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104787","id":3050334103,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc610GeX","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-08T21:21:09Z","updated_at":"2025-07-08T21:38:18Z","body":"@lyuma Skinned meshes are supposed to be untransformed direct children of the skeleton, since the only transformation comes from the bones. Your concern would only apply if a single glTF node is serving both as a bone and a mesh. However, I'm not sure if that is even a valid structure considering that bones need to be transformable, yet the transform of a skinned mesh node is ignored. The glTF validator will even warn you about this if you try it. Also, I don't think Godot or Blender lets you make glTF files with a single node as both bone and mesh, so I would be surprised if such files exist in the wild. Can you give an example file which is wrong with this PR and correct with master?\r\n\r\nI'm concerned that the slight possibility, of some likely invalid edge case, that the ecosystem actively discourages from existing, being imported slightly suboptimally... results in blocking progress on real-world bugs users are having.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3050334103/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3050509676","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104787#issuecomment-3050509676","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104787","id":3050509676,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc610xVs","user":{"login":"MeanBeanMachine2024","id":142996610,"node_id":"U_kgDOCIX0gg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/142996610?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeanBeanMachine2024","html_url":"https://github.com/MeanBeanMachine2024","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeanBeanMachine2024/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeanBeanMachine2024/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeanBeanMachine2024/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeanBeanMachine2024/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeanBeanMachine2024/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeanBeanMachine2024/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeanBeanMachine2024/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeanBeanMachine2024/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeanBeanMachine2024/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-08T23:02:23Z","updated_at":"2025-07-08T23:02:23Z","body":"@fire I don't see why it can't be merged in the beta stage if it's not release blocker since it's still a bugfix, not a feature\r\n\r\nAnd honestly it kinda should be a release blocker, it's real important to my workflow","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3050509676/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3050894606","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104787#issuecomment-3050894606","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104787","id":3050894606,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc612PUO","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-09T02:22:22Z","updated_at":"2025-07-09T02:22:22Z","body":"@MeanBeanMachine2024 That's not what release blocker means. Release blocker is for critical regressions, things that used to work but don't work anymore, which would make upgrading a bad choice for users.\r\n\r\nThis bug fix is fixing something that has never worked, therefore even without this fix, Godot 4.5 won't be worse than Godot 4.4 which also doesn't have this fix.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3050894606/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3050906465","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104787#issuecomment-3050906465","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104787","id":3050906465,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc612SNh","user":{"login":"MeanBeanMachine2024","id":142996610,"node_id":"U_kgDOCIX0gg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/142996610?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeanBeanMachine2024","html_url":"https://github.com/MeanBeanMachine2024","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeanBeanMachine2024/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeanBeanMachine2024/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeanBeanMachine2024/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeanBeanMachine2024/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeanBeanMachine2024/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeanBeanMachine2024/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeanBeanMachine2024/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeanBeanMachine2024/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeanBeanMachine2024/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-09T02:31:39Z","updated_at":"2025-07-09T02:31:39Z","body":"Dang didn't know that's how it worked, really sorry for derailing then","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3050906465/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3532149253","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104787#issuecomment-3532149253","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104787","id":3532149253,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SiFIF","user":{"login":"lyuma","id":39946030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ2MDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma","html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-14T10:48:48Z","updated_at":"2025-11-14T10:48:48Z","body":"I want to check in on this and see if this is something we want to fix for Godot 4.6.\r\n\r\nMy main issue has been that the PR breaks the case you note here:\r\n\r\n> Your concern would only apply if a single glTF node is serving both as a bone and a mesh. However, I'm not sure if that is even a valid structure considering that bones need to be transformable, yet the transform of a skinned mesh node is ignored. \r\n\r\nThis is indeed possible. I can reproduce such exports from Unity or other editors which use nodes for skinning instead of armatures/skeletons.\r\n\r\nYou are correct that the transform of the skinned mesh node is ignored for the mesh, but it is not ignored for the node hierarchy (child nodes).\r\nThe exact wording of the spec is \"[Section 3.7.3.2 Joint Hierarchy Paragraph 3](https://registry.khronos.org/glTF/specs/2.0/glTF-2.0.html#joint-hierarchy): Only the joint transforms are applied to the skinned mesh; the transform of the skinned mesh node MUST be ignored.\" -> The semicolon indicates the second part of the sentence is in the context of the first part of the sentence: namely, because only joint transforms are used for the mesh itself, the skinned mesh node's transform is ignored for the mesh.\r\n\r\nIt doesn't say that the node's transform is ignored for the purposes of other glTF functionality, nor that the node's transform must be identity. That said, I understand there is some confusion because of a warning in the glTF validator. I believe this is intended to be informational (just double checking that this is what you intended). Furthermore, I can construct a glTF document which has identity transforms for the skinned mesh node and still is used as a joint which will not emit a warning in the validator.\r\n\r\nAs for real world cases, there is a Godot issue from a user who encountered the case of skinned mesh node being used as joint in their own project, so at least one occurrence of this has existed in the real world.\r\n\r\nSo basically I'd like to see the PR changed in such a way that it can track which properties affect the translation/rotation/scale of the node, and which properties affect the mesh part of the node, since the two may become separate Godot nodes during import.\r\n\r\n(Eventually we could also see the same issue for glTF nodes which have multiple of \"camera\", \"KHR_lights_punctual\", \"mesh\", \"OMI_physics_shape\" etc. fields, if they get broken up into multiple Godot nodes for each function.)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3532149253/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]